# Astro builds directory-format pages (`dist/th/index.html`), so the one real
# address of every page ends in a slash. Cloudflare's default HTML handling
# already answers `/th` with a temporary 307 hop; these rules make it a
# permanent 301 and cover the slash-less variants Google had already indexed,
# so the two forms consolidate onto a single URL instead of competing.

/    /th/    301

/th  /th/    301
/zh  /zh/    301
/en  /en/    301

/th/transport  /th/transport/  301
/zh/transport  /zh/transport/  301
/en/transport  /en/transport/  301

/th/legal  /th/legal/  301
/zh/legal  /zh/legal/  301
/en/legal  /en/legal/  301
